    Revision: eb4142ee12ea28f796c07f475a24a1d0c66aa8f0 (2026-11-25)
    Files:    src/loaders/smc/stream.rs  ->  crates/opencheck-smc/src/stream.rs
              src/loaders/smc/mesh.rs    ->  crates/opencheck-smc/src/mesh.rs

Open BIM Suite worked out how such a file is built (a zip around one Java
object stream of the model checker's own classes) and wrote the reader of
that stream and the tessellation of its shapes. OpenCheck would not read these
files without that work.

What OpenCheck changed in the copied files (each change is marked
"OpenCheck:" in the source; the files are otherwise as upstream, run through
rustfmt with OpenCheck's settings):

- mesh.rs: the positions of a mesh are kept as f64 instead of f32, so the
  coordinates of a georeferenced model (hundreds of kilometres from the
  origin) keep their precision.
- stream.rs: a model record also keeps the file it came from (`file`), so
  the models get the names of their IFC files.

What OpenCheck added (src/lib.rs, src/ifc.rs, under the same licence as this
crate): the writing of each model as an IFC4 file, which the rest of OpenCheck
reads as it reads any IFC. The reading of the file's issues (presentations)
that Open BIM Suite also does is not taken over.

